# Task 14a fix round 1 (ba598f374f, a3e8bd7665)
commit ba598f374f86e0b875b9fa53acd379fe2218be94
Author: Richard <richard@Richards-Mac-mini.local>
Date:   Mon Oct 19 11:08:39 2026 +0700

    fix(shellx): harness stop signal survives wait_until; app-bridge checks; one-Mac environments
    
    Task 14a review fix round 1 (harness and its binary-free pins):
    - `Stopped` is a BaseException (like KeyboardInterrupt): Ctrl-C/SIGTERM
      during --app-bridge setup was swallowed by wait_until's `except Exception`
      and the harness then held forever. SIGHUP stops it too (STOP_SIGNALS).
      Pinned: wait_until lets Stopped through, and a real SIGTERM/SIGHUP during
      wait_until propagates.
    - --app-bridge makes the socket path absolute and refuses missing or
      non-executable binaries with exit 2 before starting anything (pinned).
    - MacEnv: installs on one Mac share HOME, TMPDIR and XDG_RUNTIME_DIR while
      every explicit path stays their own (Machine.paths() vs env_dirs(), pinned).
    - session_daemon_pids runs ps with PATH=MIN_PATH, LC_ALL=C, cwd=root;
      viewer_ok is False on a CLI timeout (pinned); process_log() reads a
      process's redacted log.
    - enroll_flags() pinned against the Swift enroll array; swift_array and the
      connect flag pin read the function body up to the next blank line (the
      Task 13 merge added builders after connect, which broke the old slice).
    - Module and start_host_daemon docstrings state the real stop/mint order.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

